WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 9 Student Video
Unit 3, Lesson 1: Science

1
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:18.180
Have you ever felt like your faith is threatened when you walk into a science

2
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:22.900
classroom? Maybe you've felt like science and faith are at odds.

3
00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:26.920
Or maybe you've even heard the narrative that science and faith are at war.

4
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:32.240
Should we feel like our religious beliefs are threatened when we walk into a science

5
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:37.080
classroom? Well, it's easy to think that we ought to check our religious beliefs at

6
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.860
the door when we come into the arena of science.

7
00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:44.860
But as tempting as this may be, this is not an option for a thoughtful Christian.

8
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.840
You might be pleasantly surprised to discover that it's actually the Christian

9
00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:54.320
worldview that is largely responsible for the birth of science.

10
00:00:54.620 --> 00:01:00.440
You see, there are certain ideas within the Judeo-Christian tradition that gave both

11
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:05.120
the motivation and the intellectual backing for the birth of modern science.

12
00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:10.540
Many scientific pioneers, if not most scientific pioneers,

13
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:15.500
were motivated to do science because of their theistic and in particular Christian

14
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:21.360
belief system. Scientific pioneers like Copernicus, Boyle, Galileo,

15
00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:27.440
Kepler, Newton, and many more did science because of their Christian

16
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:27.840
worldview.

17
00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:33.440
Francis Bacon believed God meant for us to explore the many mysteries that filled

18
00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:39.000
the natural world. Kepler wrote, the chief aim of all investigations of the

19
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:44.500
external world should be to discover the rational order which has been imposed on it

20
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.700
by God in which he revealed to us in the language of mathematics.

21
00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:53.600
Newton believed his scientific discoveries offered convincing evidence for the

22
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.660
existence and creativity of God.

23
00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:01.240
This most beautiful system of sun, planets, and comets could only proceed from the

24
00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:05.060
counsel and dominion of an intelligent and powerful being.

25
00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:11.520
There are three main reasons why the scientific revolution took place in a culture

26
00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.980
shaped by a theistic worldview. The first reason is that Christianity in particular

27
00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:22.520
teaches that God is orderly, he's rational in his very being, and the universe is

28
00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:27.220
orderly. And since we're made in God's image we are capable of understanding the

29
00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:31.460
world in which we live. The world is not chaotic, it's orderly.

30
00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:34.980
Second, Christianity sanctioned science.

31
00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:40.980
In other words, science was done to care for and alleviate the suffering of human

32
00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:44.240
beings and to protect and care for creation.

33
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:50.320
And third, Christianity gave the motivation is that science was to be done to bring

34
00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:51.940
glory to God.

35
00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:57.240
Despite the common narrative that we hear that science is at odds with faith.

36
00:02:57.380 --> 00:03:02.920
It's actually the Christian worldview that contributed enormously to the rise of

37
00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:03.380
science.

38
00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.020
Naturalism actually undermines science.

39
00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:12.820
Charles Darwin once said, but then with me the horrid doubt always arises whether

40
00:03:12.820 --> 00:03:17.080
the conviction of man's mind, which has been developed from the mind of lower

41
00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:20.180
animals, are of any value or at all trustworthy.

42
00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.900
Would anyone trust in the convictions of a monkey's mind if there are any

43
00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:26.800
convictions in such a mind?

44
00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:32.680
In other words, what Darwin is saying is that his very naturalistic evolutionary

45
00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:38.640
theory undermines any basis we have for concluding that evolution is true.

46
00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:44.380
Now here's why. According to this naturalistic theory, the brain is the result of

47
00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:47.420
this blind purposeless material process.

48
00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:51.780
It's a large accident. So this raises a troubling question.

49
00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:57.040
How do you know we can trust anything that the brain tells us is true?

50
00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:02.120
Now, this isn't a problem for the Christian worldview because God is reasonable, the

51
00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:06.940
world is orderly, and we've been made in God's image to understand the world in

52
00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:12.260
which we're placed. You see, naturalists can do science, but they have to borrow

53
00:04:12.260 --> 00:04:17.860
from the Judeo-Christian worldview to do so. Science and faith are not

54
00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:22.380
at odds. Now there certainly are distinct scientific and distinct theological

55
00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:27.460
questions. For example, in science, the question of how many oxygen atoms are in a

56
00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:32.760
water molecule, or in theology, what is the nature of an angel? Those are distinct

57
00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:36.760
questions that belong in their own discipline, but there are times when science

58
00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:42.580
and theology overlap. Questions such as the origin of the universe, the origin

59
00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:45.540
of mankind, and the historical resurrection.

60
00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.220
Sometimes science and faith intersect.

61
00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:53.760
The idea that Christianity is at war with science is mistaken.

62
00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:59.660
It's a misreading of the historical, scientific, theological, and philosophical

63
00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:05.340
evidence. You see, Christians have always taught that God speaks through two books,

64
00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:07.840
the book of nature and the book of scripture.

65
00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:12.920
The book of nature means that God has made himself known in creation.

66
00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:19.060
Creation speaks truths about the creator but God also has made himself known through

67
00:05:19.060 --> 00:05:25.000
the scriptures. God's word reveals truth about his character and also his design for

68
00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:30.040
mankind. Now we can certainly misinterpret the scriptures and we can misunderstand

69
00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:35.880
the scientific evidence. But when done accurately, both books reveal truths

70
00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:37.300
about the Creator.

